From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: 059 允许把 RAM code 下到 patch 用过的那个地址

Every download that ever moved the ring went to 0x00900000, the ROM patch
window; every download that stalled went to 0x00912c00, where the RAM code
header says it belongs.  Size is ruled out (12 KB stalls there too), so the
target address is the next thing to separate from the mode word.

diag_ram_addr_override downloads every RAM region to the given address
instead of the one the header declares, and logs the substitution, so one
boot can tell whether the receiver refuses the window or the request.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -443,6 +443,12 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_ram_mode_and,
 		 "AND the RAM download mode word with this value");
 
+/* 059: the only address that has ever accepted a download is the patch one. */
+static unsigned int diag_ram_addr_override;
+module_param(diag_ram_addr_override, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_ram_addr_override,
+		 "download every RAM region to this address instead (0 = as declared)");
+
 static u32
 mcu_wm_gen_dl_mode(u8 feature_set, bool is_wa)
 {
@@ -514,6 +520,13 @@
 		len = le32_to_cpu(region->len);
 		addr = le32_to_cpu(region->addr);
 
+		if (diag_ram_addr_override) {
+			dev_info(dev->dev,
+				 "diag ram addr: 0x%08x -> 0x%08x\n",
+				 addr, diag_ram_addr_override);
+			addr = diag_ram_addr_override;
+		}
+
 		if (region->feature_set & FW_FEATURE_OVERRIDE_ADDR)
 			override = addr;
 
